WEBVTT

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:08.269
Ah!

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:10.138
Surprised?

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:18.048
What's wrong?

00:00:18.118 --> 00:00:21.576
Can't figure out
why I'm still not running, huh?

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:23.383
Can't read my thoughts?

00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:30.496
Go ahead. Attack!

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:32.463
Take my ship.

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:33.794
Damn ship!

00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:35.459
Hold together.

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:36.763
Hold.

00:00:39.406 --> 00:00:43.035
Ah! Ah!

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:47.163
Wormhole?

00:02:48.368 --> 00:02:50.063
Approximately
400 million kilometers

00:02:50.136 --> 00:02:51.364
from our current position.

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:53.132
Take a look at the
transkinetic vector.

00:02:53.206 --> 00:02:56.266
It leads to Sector 001.

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:57.604
It looks like a wormhole,

00:02:57.677 --> 00:03:00.305
but we're detecting
massive bioplasmic activity.

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:01.642
That suggests a life-form.

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:03.147
Neutrino flux?

00:03:03.216 --> 00:03:04.478
Erratic.

00:03:04.551 --> 00:03:06.644
A direct route
to Earth's doorstep

00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:07.913
out of the blue.

00:03:08.054 --> 00:03:10.079
What's wrong with this picture?

00:03:10.156 --> 00:03:11.817
We should launch a probe.

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:13.256
Go to Yellow Alert.

00:03:13.326 --> 00:03:15.294
Prepare a class-5 probe.

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:17.852
Let's see
what's really out there.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:22.565
Daily Log, Seven of Nine.

00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:25.035
While we failed to locate
a new source of deuterium,

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:26.799
our mission had
educational value

00:03:26.873 --> 00:03:28.807
for at least
one member of the crew.

00:03:30.777 --> 00:03:32.142
If you go looking
for deuterium tomorrow,

00:03:32.212 --> 00:03:33.304
can I come?

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:35.574
Well, that's up to the Captain.

00:03:35.648 --> 00:03:38.708
It's likely you'll be replaced
by a more experienced officer.

00:03:38.785 --> 00:03:40.446
But this is
my first away mission

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:42.181
and I didn't get
to do anything.

00:03:42.255 --> 00:03:43.517
I disagree.

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:46.218
You familiarized yourself
with this vessel.

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:49.227
Well, can't we make first
contact with somebody

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:50.819
or get in a space battle?

00:03:50.897 --> 00:03:51.921
Yeah...

00:03:51.998 --> 00:03:52.930
can't we?

00:03:52.999 --> 00:03:54.432
Another time, perhaps.

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:57.828
Hey, Naomi,
you want to take the helm?

00:03:57.904 --> 00:03:58.836
Can I?

00:03:58.905 --> 00:03:59.837
Ensign.

00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:01.339
She'll be familiarizing herself

00:04:01.407 --> 00:04:02.897
with the vessel.

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:04.304
Here.

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:05.810
Okay.

00:04:05.878 --> 00:04:08.904
First, bring us up
to one-quarter impulse.

00:04:08.982 --> 00:04:11.348
Hit this control,
then that one.

00:04:12.719 --> 00:04:14.243
One-quarter impulse, aye.

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:17.653
Now, you think you can chart
a course back to Voyager?

00:04:17.724 --> 00:04:18.850
Yes, sir.

00:04:31.571 --> 00:04:32.663
They're in a hurry.

00:04:32.739 --> 00:04:33.933
Crewmen Boylen and White...

00:04:34.073 --> 00:04:35.938
frequently late
for their duty shifts.

00:04:36.075 --> 00:04:37.508
Ah.

00:04:37.577 --> 00:04:39.943
Speaking of late,
I'll make a deal with you.

00:04:40.079 --> 00:04:41.376
I'll explain to Sam

00:04:41.447 --> 00:04:43.915
why her daughter's
two hours late for bedtime

00:04:43.983 --> 00:04:45.848
if you start
on the survey report.

00:04:45.918 --> 00:04:47.180
Acceptable.

00:04:47.253 --> 00:04:48.379
Have fun.

00:04:56.062 --> 00:04:57.154
You're back.

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:58.663
I was beginning to worry.

00:04:58.731 --> 00:05:01.131
The survey took longer
than expected.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.498
Lucky our deuterium shortage
is no longer an issue.

00:05:04.871 --> 00:05:06.031
A wormhole.

00:05:06.105 --> 00:05:07.299
The wormhole.

00:05:07.373 --> 00:05:09.500
It leads all the way
back to Earth.

00:05:09.575 --> 00:05:11.907
The odds of finding
such a phenomenon

00:05:11.978 --> 00:05:13.172
are infinitesimal.

00:05:13.246 --> 00:05:15.441
Never bet against the house.

00:05:19.052 --> 00:05:20.314
What are you doing?

00:05:20.386 --> 00:05:22.183
Looking for anomalous readings.

00:05:22.255 --> 00:05:23.916
You will find none.

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:25.719
He's right...
no subspatial contortions,

00:05:25.792 --> 00:05:26.884
no temporal variance.

00:05:26.959 --> 00:05:28.449
The probe we sent in has already

00:05:28.528 --> 00:05:30.655
picked up faint signals
from the other side.

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:32.425
B'Elanna's still
downloading them,

00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:34.864
but she's pretty sure
they're from Starfleet.

00:05:34.934 --> 00:05:37.698
This wormhole is only
300 million kilometers away.

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:40.466
Long-range scans
should've detected it days ago.

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:42.531
Perhaps it was
an oversight on your part.

00:05:42.608 --> 00:05:45.634
If it'll make you feel
better, run a diagnostic.

00:05:45.712 --> 00:05:48.203
In the meantime,
let's maintain course.

00:06:04.964 --> 00:06:07.125
Come in.

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:08.895
I've completed my diagnostic.

00:06:08.968 --> 00:06:10.993
Sensors are operating
at peak efficiency.

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:12.230
Then there's nothing
to worry about.

00:06:12.305 --> 00:06:13.533
On the contrary.

00:06:13.606 --> 00:06:16.200
The wormhole's neutrino levels
are extremely erratic.

00:06:16.275 --> 00:06:18.038
I thought so, too...

00:06:18.111 --> 00:06:20.204
until I received this.

00:06:20.279 --> 00:06:22.679
It turns out those faint signals
we detected

00:06:22.749 --> 00:06:24.444
were communiqués from Starfleet.

00:06:24.517 --> 00:06:27.816
They assure me the neutrino flux
is nothing to worry about.

00:06:27.887 --> 00:06:29.047
Starfleet may be in error.

00:06:29.122 --> 00:06:30.384
We should run further scans.

00:06:30.456 --> 00:06:33.914
No time.
The wormhole might destabilize.

00:06:33.993 --> 00:06:37.019
The Doctor often instructs me
"to look before I leap."

00:06:37.096 --> 00:06:41.032
It is an antiquated adage,
but I believe it is relevant.

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:42.533
I have another one for you...

00:06:42.602 --> 00:06:44.035
"He who hesitates is lost."

00:06:44.103 --> 00:06:45.229
Captain...

00:06:45.304 --> 00:06:47.772
I think we're avoiding
the real issue here, Seven.

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:49.398
You're still feeling
uncomfortable

00:06:49.475 --> 00:06:51.272
about returning
to the Alpha Quadrant.

00:06:51.344 --> 00:06:52.777
It's nothing to be ashamed of.

00:06:52.845 --> 00:06:55.780
Trust me. You're going
to thrive on Earth

00:06:55.848 --> 00:06:58.282
just as you've thrived
on Voyager.

00:06:59.352 --> 00:07:00.319
Yes?

00:07:01.354 --> 00:07:03.219
Letter number two.

00:07:03.289 --> 00:07:05.280
I'm getting jealous.

00:07:08.194 --> 00:07:10.628
Mark.

00:07:10.696 --> 00:07:13.187
Apparently his engagement
was broken off.

00:07:13.266 --> 00:07:14.733
What about you?
Any news?

00:07:14.801 --> 00:07:17.201
A full pardon and
reinstatement to Starfleet.

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:19.238
I've even been offered
a professorship

00:07:19.305 --> 00:07:20.897
in anthropology at the Academy.

00:07:21.007 --> 00:07:24.170
Oh, Chakotay, congratulations,
but it's not fair.

00:07:24.243 --> 00:07:25.904
Don't worry.
It's only part-time.

00:07:26.012 --> 00:07:28.003
How am I expected to run
a ship without you?

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:29.741
You'll do fine.

00:07:38.891 --> 00:07:40.825
Computer, access all log entries

00:07:40.893 --> 00:07:43.623
recorded by Captain Janeway
on stardate 52542.

00:07:43.696 --> 00:07:46.722
Access to those files
is restricted.

00:07:59.312 --> 00:08:01.280
Access granted.

00:08:03.483 --> 00:08:05.417
Play first log entry.

00:08:05.485 --> 00:08:09.649
Captain's Log, Stardate 52542.3.

00:08:09.722 --> 00:08:12.714
Long-range sensors have
identified a wormhole

00:08:12.792 --> 00:08:14.453
leading to the Alpha Quadrant.

00:08:14.527 --> 00:08:17.394
Unfortunately,
secondary scans have revealed

00:08:17.463 --> 00:08:19.761
that it's some kind
of elaborate deception.

00:08:19.832 --> 00:08:21.823
The question is:

00:08:21.901 --> 00:08:25.200
Who's attempting to deceive us
and why?

00:08:26.606 --> 00:08:28.039
Play next log entry.

00:08:28.107 --> 00:08:29.802
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:08:29.876 --> 00:08:33.869
We've begun to receive
faint telemetry from our probe.

00:08:33.946 --> 00:08:36.813
I don't want to get
the crew's hopes up,

00:08:36.883 --> 00:08:41.013
but B'Elanna thinks it may be
a message from Starfleet.

00:08:41.087 --> 00:08:42.577
I'm beginning to wonder

00:08:42.655 --> 00:08:44.816
if my earlier skepticism
was justified.

00:08:46.225 --> 00:08:47.487
Play next log entry.

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:49.050
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:08:49.128 --> 00:08:51.688
I've set a course
for the wormhole.

00:08:51.764 --> 00:08:55.825
With any luck, we should be
back in the Alpha Quadrant

00:08:55.902 --> 00:08:57.870
in a matter of days.

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:06.300
Annika!

00:09:06.379 --> 00:09:07.971
Annika Hansen!

00:09:08.047 --> 00:09:09.844
There is no one here
by that name.

00:09:09.916 --> 00:09:10.883
Are you sure?

00:09:10.950 --> 00:09:12.975
Because I have a letter
here addressed to her.

00:09:15.688 --> 00:09:16.620
I never realized

00:09:16.689 --> 00:09:18.714
you knew anyone
from the Alpha Quadrant.

00:09:18.791 --> 00:09:19.723
I don't.

00:09:19.792 --> 00:09:22.022
Well, it looks like
someone knows you.

00:09:22.094 --> 00:09:24.187
Who's it from?

00:09:26.265 --> 00:09:27.892
Claudia Hansen.

00:09:28.034 --> 00:09:29.899
She claims to be
a sister of my father.

00:09:30.036 --> 00:09:31.901
Your aunt.

00:09:32.038 --> 00:09:34.598
She is looking forward
to meeting me.

00:09:34.674 --> 00:09:37.006
That's great!

00:09:37.076 --> 00:09:38.737
Starfleet's appointed me

00:09:38.811 --> 00:09:40.836
Ambassador
to the Lan'Tuan sector.

00:09:40.913 --> 00:09:42.175
Ambassador?

00:09:42.248 --> 00:09:46.241
I guess they thought I'd
have a flair for quadrupeds.

00:10:00.566 --> 00:10:03.330
Ensign, I require
a moment of your time.

00:10:03.402 --> 00:10:05.165
Sure.

00:10:05.237 --> 00:10:06.704
Have you noticed
anything unusual

00:10:06.772 --> 00:10:09.036
about the crew's behavior
since we returned?

00:10:09.108 --> 00:10:11.042
Like?

00:10:11.110 --> 00:10:12.907
When I presented
the Captain with evidence

00:10:12.979 --> 00:10:15.140
that the wormhole may not
be what it appears to be,

00:10:15.214 --> 00:10:16.647
she seemed unconcerned.

00:10:16.716 --> 00:10:19.241
Really? That doesn't
sound like her.

00:10:19.318 --> 00:10:20.250
I believe the crew

00:10:20.319 --> 00:10:22.048
is being deceived
by false telemetry,

00:10:22.121 --> 00:10:24.316
as well as overly-optimistic
correspondence.

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:26.324
The letters from home?

00:10:26.392 --> 00:10:28.326
I got one, too.

00:10:28.394 --> 00:10:30.328
No doubt containing good news.

00:10:30.396 --> 00:10:31.863
Oh, I'll say.

00:10:31.931 --> 00:10:33.865
An old buddy of mine
offered me a spot

00:10:33.933 --> 00:10:36.060
at the new test flight center
in Australia.

00:10:36.135 --> 00:10:38.069
Beautiful beaches,

00:10:38.137 --> 00:10:41.436
a chance to pilot
the latest experimental ships.

00:10:41.507 --> 00:10:42.735
I can't believe it.

00:10:42.808 --> 00:10:44.833
Then you doubt the veracity
of the letters as well.

00:10:44.910 --> 00:10:46.844
Are you kidding?

00:10:46.912 --> 00:10:50.109
I've already written back
and accepted the job.

00:10:57.423 --> 00:10:59.448
Computer, activate the EMH.

00:10:59.525 --> 00:11:01.891
Please state the nature
of the medical emergency.

00:11:01.961 --> 00:11:03.929
The wormhole is not
what it appears to be.

00:11:04.063 --> 00:11:05.758
I believe that the crew
is being...

00:11:05.831 --> 00:11:07.264
Hold on. Wormhole?

00:11:07.333 --> 00:11:08.630
You weren't informed.

00:11:08.701 --> 00:11:10.032
Not a peep.

00:11:10.102 --> 00:11:11.933
Considering
everyone's recent behavior,

00:11:12.071 --> 00:11:13.504
that's not surprising.

00:11:13.572 --> 00:11:15.199
Since the discovery
of this wormhole,

00:11:15.274 --> 00:11:18.038
the crew has ignored obvious
signs that it's a deception.

00:11:18.110 --> 00:11:20.101
You must determine if there is
a physiological explanation.

00:11:20.179 --> 00:11:21.942
Seven of Nine to the Bridge.

00:11:22.014 --> 00:11:24.278
On my way.

00:11:24.350 --> 00:11:27.615
I'll call in a few crewmen
for routine examinations.

00:11:27.687 --> 00:11:30.713
That should allow me to run
the necessary diagnostics.

00:11:37.029 --> 00:11:38.690
We've just entered
visual range.

00:11:38.764 --> 00:11:40.698
I thought you'd like
to take a look.

00:11:40.766 --> 00:11:44.725
We're starting to get images
from the other side.

00:11:44.804 --> 00:11:46.829
There is
considerable interference.

00:11:47.907 --> 00:11:50.671
I think I can help clear it up.

00:11:53.079 --> 00:11:54.376
Try it now.

00:12:12.798 --> 00:12:14.527
How long
until we reach the wormhole?

00:12:15.601 --> 00:12:17.466
53 minutes.

00:12:17.536 --> 00:12:18.901
Maintain course.

00:12:19.972 --> 00:12:22.304
All hands, this is the Bridge.

00:12:22.374 --> 00:12:23.705
Secure all systems.

00:12:23.776 --> 00:12:26.540
When we reach Earth's orbit,
lay in a descent trajectory,

00:12:26.612 --> 00:12:29.877
North American continent,
Starfleet Headquarters.

00:12:40.392 --> 00:12:42.087
Computer,
perform a gravimetric scan

00:12:42.161 --> 00:12:44.095
of the wormhole's interior.

00:12:44.163 --> 00:12:46.495
Look for inconsistencies
in the spatial gradient.

00:12:46.565 --> 00:12:49.728
The anomaly is consistent
with a class-1 wormhole.

00:12:49.802 --> 00:12:51.326
No irregularities detected.

00:12:51.403 --> 00:12:54.463
Recalibrate sensors
and try again.

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:57.008
No irregularities detected.

00:12:59.245 --> 00:13:01.941
Isolate grid 925 and magnify.

00:13:03.849 --> 00:13:07.512
Computer, is that a vessel
in grid 91?

00:13:07.586 --> 00:13:09.178
No vessel has been detected.

00:13:11.157 --> 00:13:12.681
Open a com channel.

00:13:12.758 --> 00:13:14.191
Channel open.

00:13:14.260 --> 00:13:17.024
Alien vessel,
this is the Starship Voyager.

00:13:17.096 --> 00:13:18.791
Respond.

00:13:18.864 --> 00:13:20.354
Alien vessel...

00:13:22.868 --> 00:13:24.631
Who are you?

00:13:24.703 --> 00:13:27.263
Seven of Nine,
Federation Starship Voyager.

00:13:27.339 --> 00:13:28.806
Our ship is
on an intercept course

00:13:28.874 --> 00:13:31.240
3.4 light-years
from your position.

00:13:31.310 --> 00:13:32.937
Turn around.

00:13:33.078 --> 00:13:35.911
You're being deceived.

00:13:35.981 --> 00:13:37.209
How?

00:13:37.283 --> 00:13:39.183
He knows what you want.

00:13:45.624 --> 00:13:48.593
Computer, identify the cause
of the power failure.

00:13:48.661 --> 00:13:50.720
Captain's orders.

00:13:50.796 --> 00:13:52.525
Power from Astrometrics
has been rerouted

00:13:52.598 --> 00:13:55.089
to the navigational array,
at least until we've completed

00:13:55.167 --> 00:13:56.566
our journey
through the wormhole.

00:13:56.635 --> 00:13:59.570
I've made contact with a vessel
inside the anomaly.

00:13:59.638 --> 00:14:00.866
Starfleet?

00:14:00.940 --> 00:14:01.998
Alien.

00:14:02.074 --> 00:14:04.099
The pilot attempted
to warn us away.

00:14:09.081 --> 00:14:12.710
Sensors show no record
of an incoming transmission.

00:14:12.785 --> 00:14:14.412
The sensors are malfunctioning.

00:14:14.486 --> 00:14:16.181
He said we were being deceived,

00:14:16.255 --> 00:14:18.746
that the wormhole is not
what it appears to be.

00:14:18.824 --> 00:14:21.224
The preponderance of data
suggests otherwise.

00:14:21.293 --> 00:14:22.783
The data is flawed.

00:14:22.862 --> 00:14:25.023
As is your reasoning.

00:14:26.799 --> 00:14:29.097
May I ask you
a personal question?

00:14:31.303 --> 00:14:33.794
Are you looking forward
to seeing your wife and family?

00:14:33.873 --> 00:14:35.704
Indeed.

00:14:35.774 --> 00:14:39.403
And is that desire stronger
than you expected it to be?

00:14:39.478 --> 00:14:41.241
Your point?

00:14:41.313 --> 00:14:43.076
I believe
you are being manipulated.

00:14:43.148 --> 00:14:45.639
Someone or something
is compromising your logic.

00:14:45.718 --> 00:14:48.744
Otherwise, you would be willing
to listen to my concerns.

00:14:50.189 --> 00:14:52.157
Access to the Astrometrics Lab

00:14:52.224 --> 00:14:54.818
is restricted
until further notice.

00:14:56.829 --> 00:14:58.319
Dismissed.

00:15:48.681 --> 00:15:51.343
Naomi Wildman.

00:15:51.417 --> 00:15:53.544
Your presence here
is unauthorized.

00:15:53.619 --> 00:15:55.416
State your intentions.

00:15:55.487 --> 00:15:57.853
I'm... hiding.

00:15:57.923 --> 00:15:59.447
From whom?

00:15:59.525 --> 00:16:00.492
Everyone.

00:16:00.559 --> 00:16:02.254
They're all acting strange.

00:16:02.328 --> 00:16:03.795
Even Mom.

00:16:03.862 --> 00:16:05.727
Elaborate.

00:16:05.798 --> 00:16:08.164
She keeps smiling all the time,
talking about Earth

00:16:08.233 --> 00:16:10.360
like it's the greatest place
in the universe.

00:16:10.436 --> 00:16:14.031
You do not share your mother's
desire to return to Earth?

00:16:14.106 --> 00:16:15.903
Voyager's my home.

00:16:16.041 --> 00:16:19.636
If we go to Earth,
I'll have to leave the ship.

00:16:19.712 --> 00:16:22.442
I'd miss my room, Neelix...

00:16:22.514 --> 00:16:25.972
you and I wouldn't be able
to play Kadis-Kot anymore.

00:16:29.288 --> 00:16:30.915
Curious.

00:16:31.056 --> 00:16:34.184
You and I appear to be
the only ones not affected.

00:16:34.259 --> 00:16:35.521
Affected by what?

00:16:35.594 --> 00:16:38.654
I am not certain.

00:16:38.731 --> 00:16:41.723
Stay here until I return.

00:16:52.578 --> 00:16:54.671
Computer, activate EMH.

00:16:54.747 --> 00:16:57.545
Please state the nature
of the medical emergency.

00:16:57.616 --> 00:16:58.947
Where's the Doctor?

00:16:59.018 --> 00:17:00.076
Off-line.

00:17:00.152 --> 00:17:01.210
Why?

00:17:01.286 --> 00:17:02.344
Starfleet orders...

00:17:02.421 --> 00:17:03.979
something about the wormhole

00:17:04.056 --> 00:17:06.354
interfering with
the holographic systems.

00:17:06.425 --> 00:17:08.416
They didn't want
to damage his program.

00:17:08.494 --> 00:17:09.688
He must be reactivated.

00:17:09.762 --> 00:17:12.253
No can do, not until we're
on the other side.

00:17:12.331 --> 00:17:13.628
It's urgent.

00:17:13.699 --> 00:17:16.463
Believe it or not,
I am capable of handling

00:17:16.535 --> 00:17:19.265
almost any medical problem
you might have.

00:17:29.848 --> 00:17:32.248
I was just coming to see you.

00:17:32.317 --> 00:17:33.579
Why?

00:17:33.652 --> 00:17:36.246
I'm afraid I have
some troubling news.

00:17:36.321 --> 00:17:38.482
Evidently, our wormhole
passes through

00:17:38.557 --> 00:17:41.048
a layer of subspace
monitored by the Borg.

00:17:41.126 --> 00:17:44.118
Starfleet's concerned
that your neural transceiver

00:17:44.196 --> 00:17:46.164
might attract
some unwanted attention.

00:17:46.231 --> 00:17:48.062
We need to deactivate
your implants.

00:17:48.133 --> 00:17:49.657
You should not attempt to do so

00:17:49.735 --> 00:17:51.396
without the Doctor's
supervision.

00:17:51.470 --> 00:17:52.937
Unfortunately, he's off-line.

00:17:53.005 --> 00:17:54.734
Then the procedure
is inadvisable.

00:17:54.807 --> 00:17:57.332
Try to relax. We're only
going to keep you in stasis

00:17:57.409 --> 00:17:58.933
until we've reached
the Alpha Quadrant.

00:17:59.044 --> 00:18:00.409
I realize the prospect

00:18:00.479 --> 00:18:02.970
of returning to Earth
is frightening to you.

00:18:03.048 --> 00:18:06.074
It's perfectly natural for you
to resist the unknown,

00:18:06.151 --> 00:18:07.618
but you're in good hands.

00:18:07.686 --> 00:18:10.314
Resistance is futile.

00:18:17.296 --> 00:18:19.059
What's our distance, Tom?

00:18:21.567 --> 00:18:24.127
2,000 kilometers and closing.

00:18:24.203 --> 00:18:27.900
Good-bye, Delta Quadrant.

00:18:28.040 --> 00:18:31.999
No more Hirogen hunting parties,
Malon garbage scows.

00:18:32.077 --> 00:18:33.305
By this time tomorrow,

00:18:33.378 --> 00:18:37.212
it'll be Cardassians,
Romulans, Ferengi...

00:18:37.282 --> 00:18:38.874
Chakotay to the Bridge.

00:18:38.951 --> 00:18:40.111
Go ahead.

00:18:40.185 --> 00:18:41.846
I've spoken to Seven of Nine.

00:18:41.920 --> 00:18:43.683
We're putting her into stasis.

00:18:43.755 --> 00:18:44.847
Well, make it fast.

00:18:44.923 --> 00:18:48.256
We don't want the Borg to crash
our welcome home party.

00:18:51.096 --> 00:18:54.065
I need to adjust
my regeneration parameters.

00:18:58.470 --> 00:19:00.233
How long will I remain inactive?

00:19:00.305 --> 00:19:03.172
A couple of hours
to be on the safe side.

00:19:10.516 --> 00:19:12.347
Security alert!

00:19:14.853 --> 00:19:17.014
Naomi Wildman.

00:19:20.626 --> 00:19:21.615
Security's on their way,

00:19:21.693 --> 00:19:23.388
Chakotay.
What happened?

00:19:23.462 --> 00:19:26.898
Seven's trapped us behind
some kind of Borg force field.

00:19:26.965 --> 00:19:28.489
Try to disable it.

00:19:30.602 --> 00:19:32.160
Naomi...

00:19:32.237 --> 00:19:33.864
go back to your quarters.

00:19:33.939 --> 00:19:35.167
Pay attention to me.

00:19:35.240 --> 00:19:37.071
If this indicator
begins to flash,

00:19:37.142 --> 00:19:39.372
enter the following
series of commands.

00:19:39.444 --> 00:19:41.435
Watch carefully.

00:19:41.513 --> 00:19:42.207
Naomi.

00:19:42.281 --> 00:19:44.715
Do you understand?

00:19:44.783 --> 00:19:46.683
Yes.

00:19:46.752 --> 00:19:48.219
Naomi...

00:19:48.287 --> 00:19:50.221
I'm giving you a direct order.

00:19:50.289 --> 00:19:52.484
Step away from the console.

00:20:00.299 --> 00:20:01.926
She's blocking my commands.

00:20:03.502 --> 00:20:05.333
Keep trying.

00:20:10.275 --> 00:20:12.175
Computer, lock
onto my coordinates

00:20:12.244 --> 00:20:14.371
and initiate
a site-to-site transport.

00:20:14.446 --> 00:20:15.435
Main Engineering.

00:20:31.964 --> 00:20:33.431
Seven?

00:20:33.498 --> 00:20:35.363
I'm sorry.

00:20:45.644 --> 00:20:47.407
We've got phaser fire
in Engineering.

00:20:47.479 --> 00:20:48.969
Janeway to Security.

00:20:49.047 --> 00:20:52.483
Computer, erect a level-10
force field around Engineering.

00:20:52.551 --> 00:20:56.112
Lock out the command controls
with Borg encryption code 294.

00:20:56.188 --> 00:20:58.383
Seven's tapping
into the engine manifold.

00:20:58.457 --> 00:21:00.652
She's trying to shut down
impulse drive.

00:21:10.969 --> 00:21:12.664
Bridge.

00:21:12.738 --> 00:21:14.933
She has erected
another force field.

00:21:15.040 --> 00:21:17.270
It will require several minutes
to deactivate it.

00:21:17.342 --> 00:21:19.936
Where is she exactly?

00:21:20.078 --> 00:21:23.411
Engineering Console 16-Beta.

00:21:23.482 --> 00:21:24.949
Captain?

00:21:25.017 --> 00:21:27.383
I'm sending an EM surge
to that station.

00:21:27.452 --> 00:21:31.650
Seven's going into stasis
whether she likes it or not.

00:21:37.095 --> 00:21:38.960
She's down, Captain.

00:21:39.031 --> 00:21:40.862
Captain...

00:21:40.932 --> 00:21:42.627
we're at the threshold.

00:21:42.701 --> 00:21:45.135
Take us in.

00:22:05.223 --> 00:22:06.190
Report.

00:22:06.258 --> 00:22:09.318
It's just spatial turbulence.

00:22:09.394 --> 00:22:11.328
It's beautiful.

00:22:21.206 --> 00:22:23.470
Steady as she goes.

00:25:00.365 --> 00:25:02.128
Seven, wake up.

00:25:03.201 --> 00:25:04.600
Seven of Nine.

00:25:04.669 --> 00:25:06.261
Wake up.

00:25:09.975 --> 00:25:11.272
Force field.

00:25:30.362 --> 00:25:31.829
You are damaged.

00:25:31.897 --> 00:25:33.694
It's just a scrape.

00:25:33.765 --> 00:25:35.027
The crew?

00:25:36.568 --> 00:25:38.695
Unconscious. Sort of.

00:25:43.675 --> 00:25:45.609
Our hull is demolecularizing.

00:25:45.677 --> 00:25:47.702
Do wormholes do that?

00:25:49.281 --> 00:25:51.215
No... they don't.

00:25:51.283 --> 00:25:54.844
Return to your quarters
while I assess the situation.

00:25:54.920 --> 00:25:56.353
But I can help.

00:25:56.421 --> 00:25:59.879
My mom says two heads
are better than one.

00:25:59.958 --> 00:26:02.358
Isn't that
the Borg philosophy, too?

00:26:02.427 --> 00:26:05.157
Simplistic, but accurate.

00:26:05.230 --> 00:26:07.357
Please...
I don't want to be alone.

00:26:27.786 --> 00:26:29.310
Neelix!

00:26:34.159 --> 00:26:35.558
Oh, Neelix.

00:26:35.627 --> 00:26:38.755
He will survive.

00:26:41.433 --> 00:26:43.025
Neelix.

00:26:43.101 --> 00:26:44.659
We must keep moving.

00:26:47.072 --> 00:26:49.370
Naomi Wildman.

00:26:54.012 --> 00:26:56.674
We will return for him.

00:27:11.329 --> 00:27:14.423
I don't think that's Earth.

00:27:14.499 --> 00:27:15.693
No.

00:27:15.767 --> 00:27:17.701
So, where are we?

00:27:27.946 --> 00:27:30.210
I've restored partial systems.

00:27:31.750 --> 00:27:33.718
I'm reading
organic compounds,

00:27:33.785 --> 00:27:35.912
bioplasmic discharges,

00:27:36.021 --> 00:27:38.581
a vast network
of neural pathways.

00:27:38.657 --> 00:27:40.921
Is it a life-form?

00:27:40.992 --> 00:27:43.927
If it is,
it's the largest I've seen...

00:27:44.029 --> 00:27:46.793
over 2,000 kilometers
in diameter.

00:27:49.868 --> 00:27:51.165
What are you doing?

00:27:51.236 --> 00:27:52.897
My earlier scans
revealed a vessel.

00:27:52.971 --> 00:27:54.336
I'm trying to find it again.

00:27:54.406 --> 00:27:56.499
Somebody else is stuck here?

00:27:56.574 --> 00:27:58.405
Possibly.

00:27:58.476 --> 00:28:00.068
There.

00:28:00.145 --> 00:28:02.636
It's heavily damaged,
but still functioning.

00:28:02.714 --> 00:28:06.013
Alien vessel, respond.

00:28:07.085 --> 00:28:08.882
This is the Starship Voyager.

00:28:08.987 --> 00:28:10.477
Please respond.

00:28:14.492 --> 00:28:16.892
I told you to stay away.

00:28:16.995 --> 00:28:18.622
Why didn't you listen?

00:28:18.697 --> 00:28:20.995
Our crew believed they were
returning to their homes.

00:28:21.066 --> 00:28:24.627
Everything
they've always wanted, correct?

00:28:24.703 --> 00:28:26.671
Yes.

00:28:26.738 --> 00:28:28.467
He deceived them.

00:28:28.540 --> 00:28:30.531
"He"?

00:28:30.608 --> 00:28:32.303
I believe
we should work together

00:28:32.377 --> 00:28:33.639
to escape this anomaly.

00:28:33.712 --> 00:28:35.907
Lower your shields
and I'll beam you aboard.

00:28:36.047 --> 00:28:38.777
Shields are the only thing
holding my ship together.

00:28:38.850 --> 00:28:40.181
I'd be destroyed.

00:28:40.251 --> 00:28:42.651
I will enhance
your shield emitters.

00:28:42.721 --> 00:28:45.918
You won't fool me that easily.

00:28:46.057 --> 00:28:48.651
I assure you
we are not a deception.

00:28:48.727 --> 00:28:50.524
Oh, how convenient.

00:28:50.595 --> 00:28:54.429
An enormous starship
comes to my rescue.

00:28:54.499 --> 00:28:58.026
You might try
a more subtle approach.

00:28:58.103 --> 00:29:00.731
My scans indicate
that your shields will fail

00:29:00.805 --> 00:29:02.466
in approximately 15 minutes.

00:29:02.540 --> 00:29:05.304
Join us, or you can
remain on your vessel,

00:29:05.376 --> 00:29:07.742
secure in the knowledge
that you were not deceived,

00:29:07.812 --> 00:29:10.713
but that knowledge will do you
little good when you are dead.

00:29:13.218 --> 00:29:14.879
Decide now.

00:29:16.955 --> 00:29:18.889
All right.

00:29:20.558 --> 00:29:22.185
All right!

00:29:25.363 --> 00:29:28.332
I'm taking my shields down.

00:29:54.192 --> 00:29:55.625
Ow!

00:30:01.466 --> 00:30:04.924
You look real enough,
but over the years,

00:30:05.069 --> 00:30:09.529
he's made me believe
many things are real...

00:30:09.607 --> 00:30:11.939
a fortune at my fingertips,

00:30:12.076 --> 00:30:14.943
good friends
risen from the dead.

00:30:15.046 --> 00:30:18.038
You're referring to the anomaly
we've entered.

00:30:18.116 --> 00:30:21.051
"Anomaly"?

00:30:21.119 --> 00:30:22.416
It's a beast.

00:30:22.487 --> 00:30:23.954
Cunning, deadly.

00:30:24.055 --> 00:30:25.818
What does it want?

00:30:25.890 --> 00:30:28.415
You...

00:30:28.493 --> 00:30:30.085
your ship...

00:30:30.161 --> 00:30:32.789
antimatter, biomatter.

00:30:32.864 --> 00:30:35.458
He consumes it.

00:30:35.533 --> 00:30:37.660
Everyone believed
it was a wormhole.

00:30:37.735 --> 00:30:39.862
Hmm, telepathy...

00:30:39.938 --> 00:30:42.202
psychogenic manipulation.

00:30:42.273 --> 00:30:45.606
He senses your thoughts,
your desires,

00:30:45.677 --> 00:30:48.077
and then he preys on them.

00:30:48.146 --> 00:30:49.636
Like a pitcher plant.

00:30:50.949 --> 00:30:52.348
Pitcher plant?

00:30:52.417 --> 00:30:54.715
The Doctor taught me about it
in botany class.

00:30:54.786 --> 00:30:58.278
It catches insects
by mimicking pheromones.

00:30:58.356 --> 00:31:00.153
Yes, you're right,

00:31:00.225 --> 00:31:03.661
but this one
doesn't eat insects.

00:31:05.430 --> 00:31:09.025
He eats starships.

00:31:09.100 --> 00:31:11.694
You are familiar
with this life-form?

00:31:11.769 --> 00:31:15.603
Familiar? I've been hunting it
for nearly 40 years.

00:31:15.673 --> 00:31:18.039
And have you become impervious
to its telepathy?

00:31:18.109 --> 00:31:23.911
Almost, but there are days
when he can still trick me.

00:31:23.982 --> 00:31:25.847
Like yesterday.

00:31:25.917 --> 00:31:30.877
I thought I had found a way
to kill him once and for all.

00:31:30.955 --> 00:31:34.413
I'd allow him
to begin consuming my ship,

00:31:34.492 --> 00:31:39.486
and then I'd fly directly
to his most vulnerable system...

00:31:39.564 --> 00:31:42.397
his primary neural plexus. Boom!

00:31:42.467 --> 00:31:46.563
I'd destroy him
from the inside out.

00:31:46.638 --> 00:31:49.505
But he knew.

00:31:49.574 --> 00:31:54.910
He showed me
what I wanted to see.

00:31:54.979 --> 00:31:58.972
I was nowhere near
his neural plexus.

00:31:59.117 --> 00:32:03.679
I was flying directly
into his digestion chamber.

00:32:06.658 --> 00:32:09.593
And speaking of digestion...

00:32:09.661 --> 00:32:11.424
How do we get out
of the monster?

00:32:11.496 --> 00:32:12.929
It's not a monster.

00:32:13.031 --> 00:32:15.829
It's a bioplasmic organism,
and we will find a way out.

00:32:15.900 --> 00:32:17.390
No.

00:32:17.468 --> 00:32:20.130
The girl's right.

00:32:20.204 --> 00:32:22.104
He's a monster

00:32:22.173 --> 00:32:26.610
and the only way out
is to destroy him.

00:32:35.753 --> 00:32:38.187
Please state the nature
of the medical emergency.

00:32:38.256 --> 00:32:40.190
Your ship is being devoured.

00:32:40.258 --> 00:32:41.657
I'd say that's an emergency.

00:32:41.726 --> 00:32:45.093
The monster ate his ship, too.

00:32:45.163 --> 00:32:46.425
"Monster"?

00:32:46.497 --> 00:32:48.556
I want to see
your weapons manifest.

00:32:48.633 --> 00:32:49.691
"Weapons"?

00:32:49.767 --> 00:32:51.496
This is a Sick Bay,
not an arsenal.

00:32:51.569 --> 00:32:52.968
What's going on?

00:32:53.104 --> 00:32:55.572
Voyager has been lured
into the digestive chamber

00:32:55.640 --> 00:32:57.073
of a bioplasmic organism.

00:32:57.141 --> 00:32:59.507
We require your assistance
in charting an escape route.

00:32:59.577 --> 00:33:01.738
Slow down. The last
thing I remember

00:33:01.813 --> 00:33:03.747
I was speaking to Mr. Paris.

00:33:03.815 --> 00:33:05.908
He said the wormhole posed
a threat to my program.

00:33:05.984 --> 00:33:08.919
The beast has been
manipulating your crew.

00:33:08.987 --> 00:33:11.888
The moment he realized you were
beginning to suspect something,

00:33:11.956 --> 00:33:13.753
he made sure
you were deactivated.

00:33:13.825 --> 00:33:15.190
And who might you be?

00:33:15.259 --> 00:33:16.920
The local monster expert?

00:33:16.995 --> 00:33:20.089
As a matter of fact, I am.

00:33:20.164 --> 00:33:24.294
He's been fooling you for days,
creating false sensor readings,

00:33:24.369 --> 00:33:27.861
and he's been altering
your crew's thought patterns...

00:33:27.939 --> 00:33:32.035
a little neurogenic telepathy
to make them lower their guard.

00:33:32.110 --> 00:33:34.670
That might explain
the heightened dopamine levels

00:33:34.746 --> 00:33:37.442
I found during my "routine
examinations" of the crew.

00:33:37.515 --> 00:33:39.039
Have you informed the Captain?

00:33:39.117 --> 00:33:40.414
She's asleep.

00:33:40.485 --> 00:33:41.452
Asleep?

00:33:41.519 --> 00:33:43.214
It's our proximity
to the creature.

00:33:43.287 --> 00:33:45.187
The neurogenic field
is stronger here.

00:33:45.256 --> 00:33:47.383
It's already rendered
most of the crew unconscious.

00:33:47.458 --> 00:33:49.449
Does your vessel's database
contain information

00:33:49.527 --> 00:33:50.892
on the creature's anatomy?

00:33:50.962 --> 00:33:51.894
Of course.

00:33:51.963 --> 00:33:53.988
Retrieve it.

00:33:55.733 --> 00:33:59.726
In the meantime, let's work
on a wake-up call for the crew.

00:34:13.985 --> 00:34:15.179
Computer, increase

00:34:15.253 --> 00:34:17.881
neurotransmitter levels
by 29 percent.

00:34:17.955 --> 00:34:19.354
A cortical inhibitor?

00:34:19.424 --> 00:34:22.689
I thought it might disrupt
the organism's hold on her.

00:34:22.760 --> 00:34:23.784
It won't.

00:34:23.861 --> 00:34:26.022
I already tried
a similar procedure.

00:34:26.097 --> 00:34:28.691
I don't remember asking
for a second opinion.

00:34:29.767 --> 00:34:30.699
It's working.

00:34:30.768 --> 00:34:32.463
She's regaining consciousness.

00:34:35.573 --> 00:34:37.438
Doctor.

00:34:37.508 --> 00:34:40.568
You're being exposed to
a powerful neurogenic field.

00:34:40.645 --> 00:34:43.136
You've been unconscious
for several hours.

00:34:46.484 --> 00:34:47.951
They're here.

00:34:48.019 --> 00:34:50.351
Who?

00:34:50.421 --> 00:34:52.855
The Maquis.
They're alive!

00:34:52.924 --> 00:34:54.755
B'Elanna,
you're still on Voyager.

00:34:54.826 --> 00:34:55.884
You're hallucinating.

00:34:55.960 --> 00:34:57.791
Starfleet thinks
you've all been killed.

00:34:57.862 --> 00:34:59.796
Computer, increase
neurotransmitter levels

00:34:59.864 --> 00:35:00.796
another ten percent.

00:35:00.865 --> 00:35:01.797
What happened?

00:35:01.866 --> 00:35:03.231
B'Elanna, focus on my voice.

00:35:03.301 --> 00:35:05.292
She doesn't want to.

00:35:13.211 --> 00:35:15.577
They never want to.

00:35:35.166 --> 00:35:38.431
It's the silence I hate...

00:35:38.503 --> 00:35:42.564
the way he takes you
without a fight.

00:35:42.640 --> 00:35:45.541
It was the same way
with the Nokaro.

00:35:45.610 --> 00:35:53.210
A crew of nearly 3,000...
families mostly, mine included...

00:35:53.284 --> 00:35:57.448
looking for
a new world to settle,

00:35:57.522 --> 00:36:00.958
but they came across
our friend here

00:36:01.058 --> 00:36:03.583
and he showed them
what they wanted to see...

00:36:03.661 --> 00:36:10.032
a glistening green paradise.

00:36:10.101 --> 00:36:13.696
By the time I responded
to their distress call,

00:36:13.771 --> 00:36:15.762
all that was left of them

00:36:15.840 --> 00:36:18.400
was some fading
engine emissions.

00:36:18.476 --> 00:36:21.445
That was 39 years ago.

00:36:21.512 --> 00:36:24.743
39 years, two weeks,
four days...

00:36:24.815 --> 00:36:26.442
Do you mind?

00:36:26.517 --> 00:36:28.144
The situation is dismal enough.

00:36:28.219 --> 00:36:32.155
I'm just trying to explain
who we're up against.

00:36:32.223 --> 00:36:34.691
Well, I'm getting
a pretty good idea on my own.

00:36:34.759 --> 00:36:36.192
Judging by these bio-scans,

00:36:36.260 --> 00:36:38.319
the organism's been
devouring life-forms

00:36:38.396 --> 00:36:40.057
for a bit longer than 39 years.

00:36:40.131 --> 00:36:42.292
I'd estimate
it's at least 200,000 years old.

00:36:42.366 --> 00:36:45.460
The intelligent always survive.

00:36:45.536 --> 00:36:46.901
I wouldn't go that far.

00:36:46.971 --> 00:36:49.496
It appears to operate
on highly evolved instinct.

00:36:49.574 --> 00:36:51.769
I haven't detected
any signs of sentience.

00:36:51.842 --> 00:36:54.310
Oh, he's intelligent,
all right...

00:36:54.378 --> 00:36:58.474
smart enough to fool your crew
into taking you off-line.

00:36:58.549 --> 00:37:00.107
No need to get personal.

00:37:03.788 --> 00:37:05.016
Seven.

00:37:05.089 --> 00:37:06.420
I'm here.

00:37:09.193 --> 00:37:11.753
Are we still inside the monster?

00:37:11.829 --> 00:37:14.627
Yes, but we are going
to find a way out.

00:37:14.699 --> 00:37:16.530
There!
This is it!

00:37:16.601 --> 00:37:18.330
Exactly what we need.

00:37:21.072 --> 00:37:24.371
These class-9 torpedoes
in your weapons manifest.

00:37:24.442 --> 00:37:26.103
If we can bring
your vessel deeper

00:37:26.177 --> 00:37:28.873
into the creature's
digestive tract

00:37:28.946 --> 00:37:31.073
and detonate one
of these charges,

00:37:31.148 --> 00:37:32.809
we might be able
to destroy it.

00:37:32.883 --> 00:37:36.148
Starfleet's not in the habit
of killing life-forms.

00:37:36.220 --> 00:37:38.848
Even if that life-form
is about to kill you?

00:37:38.923 --> 00:37:40.447
If I could take a few hours

00:37:40.524 --> 00:37:42.924
to examine the creature
more thoroughly...

00:37:43.060 --> 00:37:44.391
There is no time.

00:37:44.462 --> 00:37:45.656
We kill him!

00:37:47.765 --> 00:37:49.926
Maybe there's another way.

00:37:50.001 --> 00:37:52.162
Explain.

00:37:52.236 --> 00:37:54.932
Any living organism,
no matter how large,

00:37:55.072 --> 00:37:57.563
will attempt to expel
a foreign body.

00:37:57.642 --> 00:38:01.043
If we could just make
Voyager a little less tasty...

00:38:01.112 --> 00:38:03.876
My scans indicate that your
weapons are tetryon-based.

00:38:03.948 --> 00:38:06.439
If you were to fire one
at a pocket of antimatter

00:38:06.517 --> 00:38:08.747
released from our warp core,
it would produce

00:38:08.819 --> 00:38:10.343
an electrolytic reaction.

00:38:10.421 --> 00:38:12.480
Would that
make Voyager taste bad?

00:38:13.557 --> 00:38:16.822
It might at that.

00:38:20.631 --> 00:38:22.496
Once I've beamed you
back to your ship,

00:38:22.566 --> 00:38:24.898
try adjusting your shields
to this frequency.

00:38:24.969 --> 00:38:28.370
You'll find them more resistant
to the bioplasmic discharges.

00:38:28.439 --> 00:38:30.566
You seem to know
a little about everything...

00:38:30.641 --> 00:38:34.077
medicine, exobiology,
shield harmonics.

00:38:34.145 --> 00:38:36.238
I'm something
of a renaissance EMH.

00:38:36.314 --> 00:38:38.111
I could use a crewmate like you.

00:38:38.182 --> 00:38:40.173
The beast would have
a difficult time

00:38:40.251 --> 00:38:43.118
manipulating
a hologram's desires.

00:38:43.187 --> 00:38:45.678
An Ishmael to your Ahab?

00:38:45.756 --> 00:38:47.223
No, thank you.

00:38:47.291 --> 00:38:49.885
You're turning down
the hunt of a lifetime.

00:38:49.960 --> 00:38:52.087
As appealing as that sounds,

00:38:52.163 --> 00:38:54.791
I'm a doctor,
not a dragon slayer.

00:38:54.865 --> 00:38:57.425
My program requires
that I do no harm.

00:38:57.501 --> 00:38:59.366
Shame.

00:39:16.253 --> 00:39:18.050
Qatai's vessel is ready.

00:39:18.122 --> 00:39:20.454
I've rerouted Bridge controls
to Engineering...

00:39:20.524 --> 00:39:23.186
ops, tactical, helm...
all integrated into one station.

00:39:23.260 --> 00:39:24.227
Efficient.

00:39:24.295 --> 00:39:25.592
I thought you'd like it.

00:39:25.663 --> 00:39:26.857
I'm plotting a course

00:39:26.931 --> 00:39:29.195
for the organism's
esophageal aperture.

00:39:29.266 --> 00:39:33.066
Prepare to release
the antimatter.

00:39:40.144 --> 00:39:42.908
Hull integrity's dropped
another 13 percent.

00:39:43.013 --> 00:39:44.275
Doctor.

00:39:44.348 --> 00:39:46.145
Ready on my end.

00:39:46.217 --> 00:39:48.082
Voyager to Qatai.
Prepare to fire.

00:39:52.990 --> 00:39:54.548
Wait! Wait!

00:39:55.826 --> 00:39:58.351
No, no. No, no, no.

00:39:58.429 --> 00:39:59.828
What's wrong?

00:39:59.897 --> 00:40:01.455
That last jolt

00:40:01.532 --> 00:40:05.593
must have destabilized
my targeting sensors.

00:40:05.669 --> 00:40:08.763
I could establish an interface
to Voyager's targeting array.

00:40:08.839 --> 00:40:10.932
Don't bother.
I know my ship.

00:40:11.008 --> 00:40:12.635
It's just being stubborn.

00:40:15.413 --> 00:40:17.005
Ah!

00:40:21.318 --> 00:40:22.649
Ready.

00:40:22.753 --> 00:40:25.950
Initiate the burst on my mark.

00:40:26.090 --> 00:40:27.114
Now.

00:40:37.735 --> 00:40:40.898
Like the taste of that?

00:40:40.971 --> 00:40:42.632
I'm reading violent contractions

00:40:42.706 --> 00:40:45.368
throughout
the digestive chamber.

00:40:45.443 --> 00:40:46.808
It's working.

00:40:46.877 --> 00:40:49.539
We're moving back through
the esophageal aperture.

00:40:52.983 --> 00:40:55.451
Voyager has been expelled.

00:40:55.519 --> 00:40:58.181
We're 3.9 kilometers
from the organism.

00:40:58.255 --> 00:40:59.586
After just one burst?

00:40:59.657 --> 00:41:01.249
For a big fellow,

00:41:01.325 --> 00:41:03.919
he certainly has a low tolerance
for tummy ache.

00:41:04.061 --> 00:41:05.926
Qatai's vessel was
also released.

00:41:05.996 --> 00:41:07.429
Hail him.

00:41:12.436 --> 00:41:15.337
Why haven't you ejected
a second burst?!

00:41:15.406 --> 00:41:17.203
We've cleared the organism.

00:41:17.274 --> 00:41:18.798
You've been deceived!

00:41:18.876 --> 00:41:20.901
We're both still inside it!

00:41:22.980 --> 00:41:23.912
He's right.

00:41:23.981 --> 00:41:25.608
I'm reading bioplasmic energy.

00:41:25.683 --> 00:41:29.050
I am impervious
to the creature's influence.

00:41:29.119 --> 00:41:30.177
You were impervious

00:41:30.254 --> 00:41:31.915
when it was creating
the illusion

00:41:31.989 --> 00:41:33.217
of Voyager getting home

00:41:33.290 --> 00:41:35.588
because you didn't
share that desire,

00:41:35.659 --> 00:41:38.560
but now we're trying to escape,
which is what you want.

00:41:38.629 --> 00:41:40.256
Think about it!

00:41:40.331 --> 00:41:45.359
He's showing you
exactly what you want to see.

00:41:46.704 --> 00:41:47.898
Seven!

00:41:50.808 --> 00:41:52.799
Initiate
another antimatter burst.

00:41:55.479 --> 00:41:57.071
Now.

00:41:58.182 --> 00:41:59.581
Fire.

00:41:59.650 --> 00:42:01.277
There.

00:42:13.464 --> 00:42:14.624
We're out.

00:42:14.698 --> 00:42:15.630
Are we certain?

00:42:15.699 --> 00:42:17.929
No sign of bioplasmic energy.

00:42:18.068 --> 00:42:19.126
We've escaped.

00:42:19.203 --> 00:42:21.398
I'm taking us out of range.

00:42:21.472 --> 00:42:22.496
Maximum warp.

00:42:22.573 --> 00:42:24.564
I'd better see to the crew.

00:42:26.343 --> 00:42:29.335
Well, I'll be on my way.
Thanks for your help.

00:42:29.413 --> 00:42:31.404
Your engines have taken
heavy damage.

00:42:31.482 --> 00:42:32.847
You require our assistance.

00:42:32.917 --> 00:42:33.941
No time.

00:42:34.051 --> 00:42:36.212
The beast is
already altering course.

00:42:36.287 --> 00:42:38.187
I'll handle the repairs myself.

00:42:38.255 --> 00:42:40.951
The procedure would take
several days.

00:42:41.091 --> 00:42:43.355
Don't worry about me.

00:42:43.427 --> 00:42:46.294
Just get your ship home.

00:42:46.363 --> 00:42:50.993
And watch out
for pitcher plants.

00:42:58.542 --> 00:42:59.975
Location?

00:43:00.044 --> 00:43:02.706
We're still
in the Delta Quadrant.

00:43:02.780 --> 00:43:03.872
Scan the wormhole.

00:43:03.948 --> 00:43:05.176
Find out what went wrong.

00:43:07.251 --> 00:43:09.446
It's gone.

00:43:09.520 --> 00:43:11.454
I can't find it on sensors.

00:43:11.522 --> 00:43:13.786
Captain.

00:43:13.857 --> 00:43:15.654
Bridge controls
have been routed

00:43:15.726 --> 00:43:19.253
to Engineering...
ops, tactical, helm... all of it.

00:43:19.330 --> 00:43:20.695
Bridge to Engineering.

00:43:20.764 --> 00:43:21.924
Yes, Captain.

00:43:21.999 --> 00:43:24.297
Seven? What's going on?

00:43:24.368 --> 00:43:26.029
The Doctor will explain.

00:43:26.103 --> 00:43:29.129
I will file a complete report
in the morning

00:43:29.206 --> 00:43:30.571
after I have regenerated.

00:43:31.875 --> 00:43:36.244
Captain's Log, Stardate 52542.3.

00:43:36.313 --> 00:43:38.178
We've deployed
a series of beacons

00:43:38.248 --> 00:43:41.046
to warn other vessels
about the bioplasmic creature

00:43:41.118 --> 00:43:44.246
and resumed a course for home...
our real home.

00:43:51.762 --> 00:43:53.195
Naomi Wildman.

00:43:53.263 --> 00:43:54.525
Don't worry.

00:43:54.598 --> 00:43:56.532
My presence here is authorized.

00:43:56.600 --> 00:43:57.589
By whom?

00:43:57.668 --> 00:43:59.101
Mom.

00:43:59.169 --> 00:44:01.603
She thinks I need to
learn more about Earth.

00:44:01.672 --> 00:44:03.731
I see.

00:44:03.807 --> 00:44:05.297
And does studying this image

00:44:05.376 --> 00:44:07.537
increase your desire
to go there?

00:44:07.611 --> 00:44:09.704
Not really.

00:44:09.780 --> 00:44:11.805
I concur.

00:44:11.882 --> 00:44:13.713
It is unremarkable.

00:44:13.784 --> 00:44:15.581
But my mom likes it

00:44:15.653 --> 00:44:18.417
and even Neelix can't wait
to get there,

00:44:18.489 --> 00:44:21.515
so I guess
it can't be that bad.

00:44:21.592 --> 00:44:25.323
Given this crew's determination
to return home,

00:44:25.396 --> 00:44:28.559
I have no doubt we will
see it for ourselves someday.
